Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: use the Linux 6.6 receive API for radiotap packets

Linux commit 2655926aea9b removed netif_rx_ni() in 5.18 after netif_rx()
gained support for both process and interrupt context. Keep radiotap capture
available on 6.6 using that replacement. These calls deliver monitor frames;
the ordinary Ethernet receive and WARP/HNAT fast paths are unchanged.

--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/rt_profile.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/rt_profile.c
@@ -1414 +1414 @@
-		netif_rx_ni(pOSPkt);
+		netif_rx(pOSPkt);
--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/common/sniffer_radiotap.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/common/sniffer_radiotap.c
@@ -578 +578 @@
-	netif_rx_ni(pOSPkt);
+	netif_rx(pOSPkt);
@@ -1130 +1130 @@
-	netif_rx_ni(pOSPkt);
+	netif_rx(pOSPkt);
